# APT components published to GitHub Pages by scripts/build-apt-repo.sh.
#
# One line per binary package, whitespace separated:
#   <package>  <component>
#
# Every .deb that is published must have its Package name listed here; an
# unlisted package aborts the build so a new product cannot slip in
# unclassified. Which GitHub release a .deb comes from is irrelevant — the
# split is purely by package name.
#
# main   Everything needed for a working Podman install. `apt install podman`
#        must resolve with this component alone: podman's versioned Depends on
#        netavark, aardvark-dns, containers-common and containers-storage are
#        not satisfiable from the distro archives, so they live here too.
# extra  Optional newer builds of packages whose distro versions already satisfy
#        podman's dependencies (Depends: conmon, crun | runc; Recommends: passt).
#        Add the component to pick up the current upstream releases.
podman                            main
podman-remote                     main
podman-docker                     main
netavark                          main
aardvark-dns                      main
golang-github-containers-common   main
containers-storage                main
crun                              extra
conmon                            extra
passt                             extra
